// result_end
\caption(Raw measurements, EWMA and trailing means, trailing SD, and the two directional CUSUMs.)
\alttext(Six panels compare the raw measurement series with smoothed location, dispersion and upward and downward shift statistics.)

> Interpret the chart

The raw series stays within its individual limits. EWMA starts from the
target and its limits widen as observations accumulate. The moving mean and
SD use complete trailing windows. CUSUM accumulates standardized deviations
beyond an allowance of 0.5. Its directional sums can signal sustained shifts
and continue across an alarm in this example. The plotted charts use different
memory and limit settings, so their alarm positions need not agree.

> References

- [NIST EWMA control charts|https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section3/pmc324.htm]
- [NIST tabular CUSUM|https://www.itl.nist.gov/div898/handbook/pmc/section3/pmc323.htm]
- [NIST Dataplot moving-statistic control charts|https://itl.nist.gov/div898/software/dataplot/refman1/auxillar/movecont.htm]
